8061 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ef77ed18-249f-537b-8615-5306a3284672" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128063 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128063 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128063 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4062cf11-2488-5c94-8710-b203cad7b0c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128064 #edb/ref 1080 "12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128064 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128064 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5d0de3e4-c134-5ea7-b5dc-a5a628bbec37" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129024 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8189" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129024 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR = \\Big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq \\sqrt{2y}, \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq yz \\Big\\}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129024 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7dcea6be-fd16-5312-b50c-157bafcc2d65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129024 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}{\\int }_{0}^{yz}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}[x]_{x=0}^{x=yz}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}yz\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y{[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{2y}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{y}{2}{(\\sqrt{2y})}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(8-1)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129025 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8190" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129025 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/04/043adf0ef683c24fbf4680145411d86fa94b52016bee44ac8f08ca7c5ca9f1b7.png)\n\n \n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129025 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b0ad2f24-6f0c-5d66-9312-5e41840b4fe5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129025 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/75/75a76a2dbc34c889335e66623e12b686eb9a255ee0d67f9be0e3792f2650360c.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (x,y) \\in D, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/e1/e19ffe6a0555851c2b05526272beb21dbcdc082a23a2e11809c661666efdf133.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-y}dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=4-x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-x-y)-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-x-y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(4-x)y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}((4-x)(2)-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6-2x\\,dx \\\\  & =[6x-{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(6(1)-{1}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129026 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8191" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129026 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the surface ![](images/9c/9c7c9aac6c94031d8430a8e8a2e4d3678a640379cdbc173fc5209ea532f3191b.svg) the plane ![](images/6c/6c78648d93eec934cde0f90387e06783c3d777a7a445e39afc2e5fa91bc2ec0c.svg) and the planes ![](images/89/89c97ad93c125fc2b6f61d44fe9a90845fd289329d79d506c857f970d7586540.svg) ![](images/36/36fdd3a0fb618d9692c52fd9bcb6e